WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.042 --> 00:00:02.669
If Velcro
had been invented first...

00:00:02.961 --> 00:00:04.546
-Yeah?
-...would there be zippers?

00:00:06.131 --> 00:00:08.634
You know, it's a really...
It's really a deep question.

00:00:08.717 --> 00:00:09.968
Thank you very much.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.346
I'm very excited.

00:00:14.223 --> 00:00:15.182
But there's a...

00:00:16.141 --> 00:00:16.975
There's...

00:00:17.351 --> 00:00:18.185
You see?

00:00:19.937 --> 00:00:20.771
Have a seat.

00:00:21.396 --> 00:00:23.440
Please welcome
our guest here tonight.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.319
Learn a little something&nbsp;
every day.

00:00:30.322 --> 00:00:32.950
When you're bipolar, you have
a potential to ramp up,

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:36.161
and it could take it to a point
where you start acting erratic,

00:00:36.245 --> 00:00:37.454
as TMZ would put it.

00:00:40.082 --> 00:00:42.084
Were you ostracized&nbsp;
in high school?

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:44.086
No, we'd be on dates&nbsp;
with our boyfriends,

00:00:44.169 --> 00:00:46.463
and run into the bathroom&nbsp;
and make out,

00:00:46.547 --> 00:00:48.549
and go back
to our boyfriends.

00:00:48.632 --> 00:00:50.634
I think I've had that
happen to me.

00:00:52.553 --> 00:00:53.804
Going to so many auditions,

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:56.014
I've been told,
"You're too black," "Too light,"

00:00:56.098 --> 00:00:58.016
"You're too ghetto,"
"Not ghetto enough."

00:00:58.475 --> 00:01:00.227
I've been rejected all my life.

00:01:01.311 --> 00:01:03.564
We all have
contributions to make,

00:01:03.647 --> 00:01:05.691
and we all have to look
at ourselves and say,

00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:07.526
"How do we connect&nbsp;
over our humanity?"

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.861
And then,&nbsp;
"How do we create equality?"

00:01:10.529 --> 00:01:12.364
I was a smaller kid.
Struggled at school.

00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:13.949
I was bullied
up until that point,

00:01:14.032 --> 00:01:15.867
and I get in the car, and...

00:01:16.535 --> 00:01:17.703
I was good at something.

00:01:18.787 --> 00:01:20.330
Did you have a moment
when you knew

00:01:20.414 --> 00:01:21.456
what you were gonna do?

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.667
-Mind if we talk about this?
-I'd love it.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.003
That's fairly provocative.
What happened there?

00:01:28.255 --> 00:01:29.381
Yes!

00:01:30.382 --> 00:01:32.175
Is there anything&nbsp;
we haven't covered?

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:34.094
No, I think we covered&nbsp;
a lot more

00:01:34.177 --> 00:01:36.054
than I even intended&nbsp;
on covering.

00:01:38.348 --> 00:01:40.684
Have you ever done
one of them ancestry things

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.269
-or whatever, the DNA test?
-Yeah.

00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:43.729
I wanna know if you're related

00:01:43.812 --> 00:01:45.689
to anybody
from the North Pole.

